Package: SVMC
Type: Package
Title: Structural Variation Motif Cohesion for Bacterial Genomes
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Matthew", "D'Iorio", email = "matthew.diorio@mail.mcgill.ca",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-5306-8832")))
Description: A pipeline and analysis framework for identifying, classifying,
    and validating large-scale structural variation in complete bacterial
    genome assemblies. SVMC orients genomes to OriC using multi-marker
    scoring (dnaA, DnaA-box density, GC-skew), aligns genomes with MUMmer,
    classifies five SV classes (indels, duplications, translocations,
    inversions, sub-structural inversions), and identifies lineage-defining
    motifs using a cohesion-based scoring approach validated against MASH
    distance clustering.
